  "id": "DrugBank_DB00488 - MONDO_5744",
  "verbalization": "Altretamine is suggested to have a potential role in the development of Yolk Sac Tumor through a pathway involving Tretamine. The evidence indicates that Altretamine is associated with Malignant Non-dysgerminomatous and Dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumors of Ovary, both of which are linked to Tretamine, which in turn is associated with Yolk Sac Tumor. This suggests a possible mechanistic link between Altretamine and Yolk Sac Tumor, potentially through the action of Tretamine. The observed associations are supported by a shared pathway involving Tretamine, which is a known mediator in the progression of Yolk Sac Tumor. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Altretamine to influence the development of Yolk Sac Tumor via its interaction with Tretamine, although further research is needed to confirm this relationship and elucidate the exact mechanism.",
